ilance:** Commuters should exercise extra caution when traveling, especially during and after periods of heavy rainfall. Be aware of potential signs of road instability, such as cracks, potholes, or uneven surfaces. Report any concerns to the local authorities immediately.\n\n2.  **Potential Traffic Disruptions:** Road collapses can lead to significant traffic disruptions as affected areas are closed for repairs. It's advisable to stay updated on traffic advisories issued by the Guwahati Traffic Police and plan alternative routes whenever possible. Consider using traffic navigation apps for real-time updates.\n\n3.  **Infrastructure Investment is Crucial:** This incident underscores the need for continued investment in infrastructure maintenance and upgrades across Guwahati and the North East region. Regular inspections, timely repairs, and improvements to drainage systems are essential for preventing future incidents and ensuring the safety of commuters.\n\n**Authorities Respond**\n\nLocal authorities have initiated an investigation into the road collapse to determine the precise cause and assess the extent of the damage. Efforts are underway to safely remove the trapped school bus and commence repair work on the affected section of the road. Officials have assured the public that measures will be taken to prevent similar incidents in the future.\n\nThe Guwahati incident highlights the importance of proactive infrastructure management and the need for continuous vigilance on the part of both authorities and the public. It serves as a critical reminder that ensuring safe and reliable transportation networks requires sustained investment, diligent maintenance, and a commitment to addressing potential risks before they escalate into major problems.\n\n**SEO Tags:** Guwahati road collapse, school bus trapped, Guwahati traffic, Assam infrastructure, North East India news, Guwahati news, road safety, infrastructure maintenance\n"
