d poses a significant threat to road safety. The advisory clearly states that individuals found driving under the influence will face severe legal consequences. It is crucial to designate a sober driver or utilize alternative transportation options.\n\n4.  **Use of Seat Belts and Helmets:** The use of seat belts for all passengers in a vehicle and helmets for two-wheeler riders is mandatory. These safety devices significantly reduce the risk of serious injuries in the event of an accident. Ensure that seat belts are properly fastened and helmets are securely fitted.\n\n5.  **Responsible Overtaking:** Overtaking should only be attempted when it is safe to do so, with a clear view of oncoming traffic. Avoid overtaking on blind curves, bridges, or in areas where visibility is limited. Use indicators to signal your intentions and ensure sufficient clearance before changing lanes.\n\n6.  **Avoid Distractions While Driving:** Distractions such as using mobile phones, eating, or engaging in conversations can impair a driver's ability to react to hazards. It is essential to remain focused on the road and minimize distractions while driving. Pull over to a safe location if you need to use your phone or attend to other matters.\n\n7.  **Plan Your Route and Take Breaks:** Before setting off on your picnic, plan your route in advance and familiarize yourself with the road conditions. Long drives can be tiring, so it is important to take regular breaks to rest and stretch. Avoid driving when you are fatigued or drowsy.\n\nBy adhering to these guidelines, picnic-goers can contribute to a safer and more enjoyable experience for themselves and others on the road. The Assam Police urges everyone to prioritize road safety and responsible behaviour during the picnic season.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nThe Assam Police's comprehensive road safety guidelines serve as a vital reminder of the importance of responsible driving habits. By following these rules, picnickers can ensure a safe and enjoyable experience while reducing the risk of accidents. Let's all pledge to make this picnic season a safe one for everyone on Assam's roads.\n\n**SEO Tags:** Assam road safety, picnic safety Assam, road safety guidelines, Assam travel safety, safe driving Assam, Assam picnic spots, Assam police advisory\n"
