tions:**\n\nThe removal of nearly half a million deceased voters from Assam's electoral rolls is likely to have several implications. First, it enhances the credibility of the electoral process, instilling greater confidence among voters and political parties. Second, it reduces the potential for fraudulent activities that could undermine the outcome of elections. Third, it ensures that the voter list accurately reflects the demographic reality of the state.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe Assam electoral roll revision, resulting in the deletion of 4.79 lakh deceased voters and a revised count of 2.52 crore, marks a significant step toward ensuring electoral integrity. This meticulous process underscores the commitment of election authorities to maintaining a clean and accurate voter list, fostering a more transparent and credible democratic process in the region. The updated rolls will contribute to fair and representative elections, reflecting the true will of the people of Assam.\n\n**SEO Tags:** Assam electoral roll, deceased voters removed, Assam voter list revision, Assam elections, updated voter count, electoral integrity Assam, Assam election commission, voter list accuracy\n"
